      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T23:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unless I\u0027m missing something, the Google CLA has no explicit mentions of AI. I\u0027m all for clarifying our policy/expectations around AI assisted contributions, but this feels like we might be overstating the \"need\". In general, I\u0027m hesitant to add legaese-sounding text to our docs without review from a lawyer. It\u0027s fine if we\u0027re just pointing to another legal doc (like the Google CLA) that contributors already must accept, but it\u0027s a lot iffier when it looks like we\u0027re doing interpretation of that doc. Which isn\u0027t to say we can\u0027t add rules, I just think if we\u0027re using a legal basis for the new rules, then we need legal advice. If the rules are just \"project requirements\" that we\u0027re deciding on, that feels a lot safer.",
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
