      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T23:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case you weren\u0027t aware, we already have this text in [`SUBMITTING_PATCHES`](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/changes/63/641963/18/SUBMITTING_PATCHES#58):\n```\nAll submissions to Google Open Source projects need to follow Google’s\nContributor License Agreement (CLA), in which contributors agree that\ntheir contribution is an original work of authorship. This doesn’t\nprohibit the use of coding assistance tools, but what’s submitted does\nneed to be a contributor’s original creation.\n```\n\nI think that covers a lot (but not all) of what we\u0027re trying to say below.",
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
